posts.raw:
After you left for the night we did one more with Elemental Wrath AZ, Engine of War Bunker (me), Expatriette, and Chrono Ranger vs. Iron Legacy in The Block.

&nbsp;

IL starts with -1 damage/healing, Vigilance, Heroic Redirection, and a Galvanized in play. His first card is &quot;Former Allies,&quot; which forces us to all discard a card and then lets him play another card. Unfortunately, and as I outlined in a Rules thread, that card was Rule From the Front, which did five damage (thanks to nemesis issues) to both Bunker and AZ and then made us all discard down to a single card in hand. Oh, and then of course he wallops the entire board for four, meaning that AZ and I are minus 10 hp before we even got to play anything. We&#39;re pretty sure we&#39;re boned here but might as well go ahead anyway.

&nbsp;

AZ&#39;s card is Fueled Freeze, which eliminates all of the ongoings we can destroy and ices for four, plus another three from his innate power.

My card is a Grenade Launcher for another three damage.

Expatriette has an Arsenal Access that turns up a Tactical Shotgun. Four to the face!

I don&#39;t remember what CR had (maybe Danny-Boy), but The Block took pity on us and threw up its Defensive Forcefield to buy us some time.

This basically continues for a couple turns. We never let IL flip back, but it was all we could do to hang on and keep parity with the 5HP he&#39;s regaining every turn. Chrono Ranger stuck whichever bounty gives everyone +1 damage against its target on him, offsetting his innate DR, but wasn&#39;t able to do much other than plink away. The Block thus far is a non-factor, with the Warden and a Lock Down not adding much to the proceedings.

AZ is the first to fall (perhaps not unsurprisingly, although he never actually damaged himself this game unless it was Legacy&#39;s card causing it). Turns out that his &quot;target deals itself 1 cold damage&quot; power is pretty neat when IL has out two damage pumps (the old Infection clause still works!). Expat has been working that Shotgun all day, finding a Flak Jacket that sucks up a 7-point blast from IL before donning a new one. Ranger gets his hits in when he can, including crucially getting rid of Final Evolution with a Temporal Grenade, but things are looking grim.

&nbsp;

That&#39;s when the Prison Riot happens, and we get one of the weird Time inmates, a Rogue, and of course Char. Great. (Two FILTER Agents are discarded in the chaos.)

Actually... that might just be our ticket to victory...

&nbsp;

Legacy takes no notice of them and incapacitates me before working over Expatriette some more, destroying her backup Flak Jacket. AZ makes IL self-freeze again, and I remove the Demoralizing Presense. Expat and Ranger are still shootin&#39;, and then the inmates wake up.

Well, ok first the Warden kills the weird guy, but then the Rogue takes him out. Char then deals 6 damage to the board.

That&#39;s when the [i]second[/i] Riot happens, getting the last two inmates (and dumping the remaining Agents into the trash).

&nbsp;

And they look [i]angry[/i].

&nbsp;

Legacy is still too distracted by the bullets flying at him, and finally does something about it, leaving both heroes helpless. Expat has another Access, though, which digs up an Assault Rifle, which is better than nothing. Ranger isn&#39;t able to do much but hang on, and he eventually falls when Char does his 8-damage rampage (thanks to 2 Rogues). Expartriette is down to 3hp...

&nbsp;

...but Legacy only has 1, which makes him the second-highest non-Inmate target. With the entire environment deck exhausted (and all of this happening during the Environment Start phase), the final inmate does a ton of damage to Iron Legacy and ends his tyranny.

&nbsp;

I&#39;d like to think they quietly returned to their cells after that, but it&#39;s not like Expatriette could have stopped them from doing anything else.
